# Theory and the Subject of Asian American Studies.

**Authors:** Palumbo-Liu, David

## Abstract
Addresses how significant the theoretical debates in the humanities and social sciences are for Asian American and ethnic studies and whether theory can be borrowed and applied to Asian American subjects or whether these subjects are too distinctive. The author discusses the intellectual and ideological consequences in deploying postcolonial and postmodern discourses within contemporary Asian American scholarship. (GR)

